Huh? Answer me! Fuck you!

696
01:13:50,781 --> 01:13:55,461
- What the fuck is going on?<i>- The fucking paki shot me!</i>

697
01:14:02,821 --> 01:14:05,301
Who the fuck are you?

698
01:14:07,181 --> 01:14:12,141
This looks cozy.
Where's my invite?

699
01:14:12,301 --> 01:14:17,661
- Shut up, you fucking ape.
- I'll shove this up your ass.

700
01:14:25,781 --> 01:14:29,501
That ape is coming with me.

701
01:14:29,661 --> 01:14:33,541
Yallah, Zero.
Go get him.

702
01:14:35,101 --> 01:14:38,901
What's up?
Piss off!

703
01:14:39,061 --> 01:14:41,821
Congo, go help him.

704
01:14:41,981 --> 01:14:47,021
Just stay where you are, little friend,
and no one gets hurt.

705
01:14:58,021 --> 01:15:00,141
Tough guy, huh?

706
01:15:00,301 --> 01:15:02,381
Who are you spitting at?

707
01:15:03,861 --> 01:15:07,661
Hey, Cairo.
Give your fucking car keys to Zero.

708
01:15:07,821 --> 01:15:10,821
You're fucking lucky Zuz followed you.

709
01:15:14,781 --> 01:15:17,461
- Fuck, man!
- What do you want?

710
01:15:17,621 --> 01:15:22,941
Fucking paki! Bring it on.
You've got nothing.

711
01:15:23,101 --> 01:15:25,781
Congo...

712
01:15:25,941 --> 01:15:29,621
Get into your car.

713
01:15:44,661 --> 01:15:46,981
Fuck!

714
01:16:18,781 --> 01:16:23,061
Take a shower, freshen up.
Go home to your family.

715
01:16:31,261 --> 01:16:33,821
Call me if you need anything, okay?

716
01:16:36,101 --> 01:16:39,661
No. 4 Hindbærvænget.

717
01:16:39,821 --> 01:16:43,661
- That's where Anwar is.
- What?

718
01:16:45,221 --> 01:16:47,861
What the fuck are you saying?

719
01:16:48,021 --> 01:16:51,941
Yallah, Zero.
Did you get the address?

720
01:16:52,941 --> 01:16:55,061
Anwar.

721
01:16:57,421 --> 01:16:59,741
You awake?

722
01:16:59,901 --> 01:17:02,941
My brother.
What's up, bro?

723
01:17:04,421 --> 01:17:08,181
Are we bouncing?
Should we get moving?

724
01:17:08,341 --> 01:17:13,661
Did you hit your head or something?
Hey, Anwar. Wake up.

725
01:17:16,621 --> 01:17:19,981
- Where's the coke?
- Wallah, I'm sorry, brother.

726
01:17:20,141 --> 01:17:22,621
Sorry about what?

727
01:17:22,781 --> 01:17:28,381
- Where's the coke, Anwar?
- Wallah, brother. The cops came.

728
01:17:28,541 --> 01:17:31,421
The cops came.

729
01:17:31,581 --> 01:17:36,421
Don't tell me the cops took the coke.

730
01:17:37,421 --> 01:17:42,541
You know me, brother.
Of course not. I hid it.

731
01:17:42,701 --> 01:17:45,181
The man hid the coke.

732
01:17:47,901 --> 01:17:50,621
Yallah.
Congo, get him out of here.

733
01:17:50,781 --> 01:17:53,541
Yallah.
Let's get out of this rathole.

734
01:17:53,701 --> 01:17:56,821
- Congo, I've missed you.
- I've missed you too, brother.

735
01:17:59,061 --> 01:18:01,901
Open it.

736
01:18:19,861 --> 01:18:23,621
It's Christmas morning for Daddy, huh?

737
01:18:23,781 --> 01:18:27,141
- You got off lucky.
- I told you, bro.

738
01:18:27,301 --> 01:18:30,701
We're all good. Bring the bag
and let's move, shababs.

739
01:18:30,861 --> 01:18:33,501
The streets are gonna be snowy tonight.

740
01:18:54,821 --> 01:18:57,021
<i>Amir!</i>

741
01:18:58,021 --> 01:18:59,381
<i>Amir!</i>

742
01:19:30,581 --> 01:19:33,021
<i>Yeah, bro?</i>

743
01:19:34,181 --> 01:19:37,181
I've been wondering...

744
01:19:40,981 --> 01:19:45,621
Who the fuck shows up
with a grenade like that?

745
01:19:45,781 --> 01:19:47,821
Bro...

746
01:19:47,981 --> 01:19:52,901
I saved it for a special occasion. It
finally came, thanks to your ugly face.

747
01:19:53,061 --> 01:19:56,861
Wallah, you delivered 100%.
Fucking 100%.

748
01:19:57,021 --> 01:20:00,021
Thanks for saving my ass today.

749
01:20:00,181 --> 01:20:04,261
Fuck off with that sentimental shit.
What's wrong with you?

750
01:20:04,421 --> 01:20:06,861
How's your brother?

751
01:20:07,861 --> 01:20:10,341
<i>- Abbas?</i>
- Yeah.

752
01:20:10,501 --> 01:20:15,741
He's busy. Malmö is booming.

753
01:20:15,901 --> 01:20:18,901
Nothing like here in Nørrebro.

754
01:20:20,581 --> 01:20:25,141
<i>As long as you've still got each other.
That's all that matters.</i>

755
01:20:27,941 --> 01:20:31,941
<i>- How's the family?</i>
- Total chaos.

756
01:20:34,341 --> 01:20:37,181
I don't know what to say.

757
01:20:52,341 --> 01:20:55,341
Nørrebro isn't like it used to be.

758
01:20:57,981 --> 01:21:02,541
<i>There's no place like Nørrebro.
It's home, sweet home, bro.</i>

759
01:21:03,781 --> 01:21:06,421
- Stop it.<i>- But it's true.</i>

760
01:21:07,901 --> 01:21:11,901
They've wrecked the place
with all this renovation.

761
01:21:13,061 --> 01:21:17,141
- Remember Nørrebro in our day?<i>- Yeah...</i>

762
01:21:22,781 --> 01:21:27,821
All that's left is Divan Kebab.
Number 26 with Thousand Island.

763
01:21:27,981 --> 01:21:32,021
<i>If they close, bro,
I'm out of here too.</i>

764
01:21:38,781 --> 01:21:42,981
By the way...
I was thinking about something.

765
01:21:47,861 --> 01:21:52,861
How would it work if I decided
to try out that fucking retirement?

766
01:21:57,581 --> 01:22:00,581
Then you'd tell us,
and we'd figure it out.

767
01:22:03,141 --> 01:22:05,661
<i>No stress.</i>

768
01:22:05,821 --> 01:22:10,341
<i>If that's what you want,
we'll work it out together.</i>

769
01:22:10,501 --> 01:22:12,661
Yeah, okay.

770
01:22:29,821 --> 01:22:33,701
Have you still not gotten
hold of those fucking Serbs?

771
01:22:35,581 --> 01:22:40,261
Now the coke's ready,
and they don't pick up the phone.

772
01:22:40,421 --> 01:22:45,661
Let's give it fifteen minutes, then
we'll go tell them we're ready to go.

773
01:22:49,941 --> 01:22:54,221
- Get down!
- He's in the car!

774
01:23:00,981 --> 01:23:04,901
Get him in the car. Yallah!
Get him in.

775
01:23:06,101 --> 01:23:10,461
- Yallah, get in.
- Fuck those Serbs!

776
01:23:25,261 --> 01:23:29,381
Good thing you finally
got your phone back.

777
01:23:30,541 --> 01:23:35,541
Don't you think it might be good
for you to start working again soon?

778
01:23:37,341 --> 01:23:39,341
Don't you?

779
01:23:40,781 --> 01:23:43,781
Maybe. I don't know.

780
01:23:45,221 --> 01:23:47,861
I think it would be a good idea.

781
01:23:48,021 --> 01:23:50,901
Cille, I'm saying maybe.

782
01:23:52,701 --> 01:23:55,181
I don't know.

783
01:24:04,061 --> 01:24:08,501
<i>Welcome to voicemail.
You have five new messages.</i>

784
01:24:08,661 --> 01:24:11,661
<i>To listen to your messages,
press one.</i>

785
01:24:13,741 --> 01:24:19,741
<i>First new message.
Received two days ago at 12:52 PM.</i>

786
01:24:24,581 --> 01:24:28,421
<i>Uncle? It's me, Hamza.</i>

787
01:24:30,141 --> 01:24:32,901
<i>I'm begging you. Please help me.</i>

788
01:24:33,061 --> 01:24:35,701
<i>I'm supposed to tell you to...</i>

789
01:24:54,701 --> 01:24:58,741
Who are you? Where is Hamza?

790
01:24:58,901 --> 01:25:03,981
You've got until midnight.
Otherwise Hamza dies.

791
01:25:14,101 --> 01:25:17,221
- What's the matter?<i>- I need your help, Vicki.</i>

792
01:25:17,381 --> 01:25:19,461
<i>Vicki, can you trace a number?</i>

793
01:25:19,621 --> 01:25:26,701
<i>- I need you to trace it immediately.</i>
- It could take a few days. Why?

794
01:25:26,861 --> 01:25:32,941
<i>It's about Hamza. And it's an emergency.
Find out where the SIM comes from.</i>

795
01:25:33,101 --> 01:25:36,181
<i>- And who owns it.</i>
- I'll see what I can do.

796
01:25:53,181 --> 01:25:56,581
Why are we watching
corner shop surveillance tapes?

797
01:25:56,741 --> 01:26:01,501
The provider that the number belongs to
only has three retailers in the country.

798
01:26:01,661 --> 01:26:07,061
One of them is that corner shop and
Hamza lives 300 yards down the street.

799
01:26:07,221 --> 01:26:11,541
Okay, but what are we looking for?
This is going to take hours.

800
01:26:18,741 --> 01:26:25,101
<i>Cairo, I'm having them look through
the tapes from that corner shop.</i>

801
01:26:25,261 --> 01:26:28,941
<i>We have no idea what
we're looking for, but...</i>

802
01:26:29,101 --> 01:26:33,101
<i>We've just got to stay calm.
This will take some time.</i>

803
01:27:06,101 --> 01:27:10,821
<i>- Hey, bro. What's up?</i>
- What are you up to?

804
01:27:10,981 --> 01:27:14,981
<i>Just taking care of some business.
What's going on?</i>

805
01:27:15,141 --> 01:27:19,261
Hamza's alive. I need your help.

806
01:27:19,421 --> 01:27:24,381
<i>What do you mean?
Cairo, where are you?</i>

807
01:27:24,541 --> 01:27:27,941
- The tunnel.<i>- Yallah, I'm coming.</i>

808
01:27:30,221 --> 01:27:32,341
What's up?

809
01:27:33,821 --> 01:27:37,621
- Hey, brother.
- Where's Hamza?

810
01:27:38,621 --> 01:27:43,941
- What's with the vest?
- What do you care? Where's Hamza?

811
01:27:44,101 --> 01:27:49,181
- Why the fuck are you wearing a vest?
- Is this a fucking therapy session?

812
01:27:49,341 --> 01:27:54,781
- I don't fucking have time for this.
- Aren't you fucking tired of all this?

813
01:27:56,221 --> 01:28:01,461
All these years. Aren't you tired
of constantly being on guard?

814
01:28:01,621 --> 01:28:07,501
Of not being able to take your family
to the playground without fear?

815
01:28:10,621 --> 01:28:15,661
Who the fuck kidnapped Anwar?

816
01:28:15,821 --> 01:28:19,701
Who the fuck made this mess I'm in?

817
01:28:19,861 --> 01:28:25,141
There's been nothing but trouble
since you came back, Cairo.

818
01:28:25,301 --> 01:28:30,341
That's why I'm wearing a fucking
bulletproof vest. Because of you.

819
01:28:33,661 --> 01:28:37,661
Don't forget where we fucking come from.

820
01:28:38,901 --> 01:28:44,461
Maybe you've made a nice,
peaceful life for yourself.

821
01:28:44,621 --> 01:28:48,541
Brother, look at you.

822
01:28:48,701 --> 01:28:53,501
You've turned the whole city upside down
trying to find your nephew.

823
01:28:54,741 --> 01:28:59,821
You're still the same Cairo.
Just wrapped up in fancy paper.

824
01:28:59,981 --> 01:29:03,901
You fucking bum.
Fucking idiot.

825
01:29:04,061 --> 01:29:07,021
And you're blind, brother.

826
01:29:08,181 --> 01:29:11,781
Drop this and come with me.

827
01:29:11,941 --> 01:29:15,501
Saddam, I'll tell you once.
Fucking stop this.

828
01:29:15,661 --> 01:29:18,741
Don't give me that moralizing bullshit.

829
01:29:18,901 --> 01:29:22,741
I wasn't the one who turned my back
on everyone.

830
01:29:24,021 --> 01:29:28,261
I lost my brother that night.
My fucking brother.

831
01:29:28,421 --> 01:29:30,581
My fucking brother.

832
01:29:37,861 --> 01:29:42,381
That night,
I lost both my brothers.

833
01:29:42,541 --> 01:29:45,021
Understand?

834
01:29:54,821 --> 01:29:59,581
What the fuck are we doing here?
Yallah, where's Hamza?

835
01:29:59,741 --> 01:30:01,741
Where is he?

836
01:30:01,901 --> 01:30:06,661
Why did you bring me here?
To reminisce about the old days?

837
01:30:06,821 --> 01:30:09,821
2 hours left

838
01:30:17,101 --> 01:30:19,381
"All The Way until death", huh?

839
01:30:53,141 --> 01:30:56,861
<i>Uncle? It's me, Hamza.</i>

840
01:30:58,461 --> 01:31:01,581
<i>I'm begging you. Please help me.</i>

841
01:31:01,741 --> 01:31:04,861
<i>I'm supposed to tell you...</i>

842
01:31:05,021 --> 01:31:07,741
<i>... to kill Saddam.</i>

843
01:31:10,221 --> 01:31:15,141
<i>I'm going to get killed.
Send a video once you've done it.</i>

844
01:31:15,301 --> 01:31:18,581
<i>Then you'll get the address.</i>

845
01:31:20,581 --> 01:31:25,701
22 Lundtoftegade, 2. th
Come alone

846
01:31:29,821 --> 01:31:31,901
Hey...

847
01:31:32,061 --> 01:31:34,661
- Finally someone we know.
- What?

848
01:31:34,821 --> 01:31:37,261
There. Rewind a little.

849
01:31:41,341 --> 01:31:43,541
What was the name again?

850
01:32:46,021 --> 01:32:49,101
Maryam, what am I doing here?

851
01:32:53,421 --> 01:32:56,621
Why do I have a message
with your address?

852
01:33:00,581 --> 01:33:03,581
Do you feel my pain?

853
01:33:05,021 --> 01:33:07,741
I feel your pain.

854
01:33:09,821 --> 01:33:14,061
When your child doesn't come home.
I feel for you.

855
01:33:15,501 --> 01:33:17,981
That feeling.

856
01:33:20,261 --> 01:33:23,501
My heart is burned
after what happened to my son.

857
01:33:23,661 --> 01:33:26,661
Look at the pain around you.

858
01:33:29,101 --> 01:33:33,741
Don't you think I know
you were the ones who killed my son?

859
01:33:33,901 --> 01:33:39,181
- My Younes was an innocent boy.
- No, no, no, Maryam.

860
01:33:40,181 --> 01:33:43,381
- Where is Hamza?
- You killed him.

861
01:33:44,381 --> 01:33:50,141
- You killed my son.
- Maryam, where is Hamza?

862
01:33:50,301 --> 01:33:52,861
You killed my son.

863
01:33:54,221 --> 01:33:56,061
Maryam.

864
01:33:56,221 --> 01:33:58,421
Hamza!

865
01:33:58,581 --> 01:34:01,581
Hamza! Hamza!

866
01:34:03,821 --> 01:34:07,181
Hamza! Hamza!

867
01:34:09,621 --> 01:34:12,981
Hamza! Hamza!

868
01:34:14,141 --> 01:34:16,141
Hamza!

869
01:34:16,301 --> 01:34:19,821
Where is he?
Where is Hamza, Maryam?

870
01:34:19,981 --> 01:34:22,701
He was in the stairwell.

871
01:34:22,861 --> 01:34:25,901
With that man, the criminal.

872
01:34:26,061 --> 01:34:29,981
I asked him for help with my sofa.
I needed to move it.

873
01:34:30,141 --> 01:34:33,701
Maryam, I'm serious.
Where is he?

874
01:34:33,861 --> 01:34:36,861
Hamza is a good boy.

875
01:34:41,061 --> 01:34:45,421
Enough, Maryam.
I can't lose him.

876
01:34:46,781 --> 01:34:51,221
You and your friend Saddam
are like cancer in my body.

877
01:34:51,381 --> 01:34:55,381
You poison the youth.
The children of parents.

878
01:35:00,421 --> 01:35:04,421
I still see my son in my dreams.
Do you understand?

879
01:35:06,141 --> 01:35:11,301
- You killed my son, the two of you.
- I'm sorry, Maryam. For everything.

880
01:35:11,461 --> 01:35:17,461
- Why are you upset? I lost my son.
- I'm sorry for all we did.

881
01:35:19,101 --> 01:35:24,141
- Did you know he was my only child?
- Please, tell me where Hamza is.

882
01:35:25,541 --> 01:35:27,661
I can't lose him.

883
01:35:27,821 --> 01:35:32,941
I lost my son!
I lost my only son!

884
01:35:37,181 --> 01:35:41,941
And here you are, on your knees.
What are you begging for?

885
01:35:42,101 --> 01:35:44,181
I can't lose him.

886
01:35:50,141 --> 01:35:53,381
He's in the sofa.

887
01:35:55,821 --> 01:35:58,661
Hamza!

888
01:35:59,781 --> 01:36:03,741
Hamza! Wake up!
Hamza!

889
01:36:03,901 --> 01:36:05,901
Can you hear me?

890
01:36:13,741 --> 01:36:16,061
Maryam...

891
01:36:40,061 --> 01:36:44,701
I feel sorry for your mother.
For what she will now suffer.

892
01:36:54,781 --> 01:36:59,181
It's the police!
Drop what's in your hands!

893
01:36:59,341 --> 01:37:03,341
I repeat, drop what's in your hands!

894
01:37:15,261 --> 01:37:17,101
Cairo?

895
01:37:17,261 --> 01:37:19,501
Cairo!

896
01:37:32,261 --> 01:37:37,101
I repeat, 22 Lundtoftegade.

897
01:38:59,541 --> 01:39:02,021
Who's that in the car?

898
01:39:04,221 --> 01:39:07,661
Abbas. From Malmö.

899
01:39:07,821 --> 01:39:10,301
Saddam's brother.

